# KAN-1940: CANCEL_PRINT on the first layer. The park lifts off the plate
# before any XY move, then the cut runs at the real Z and completes.
#
# CANCEL_PRINT runs PRINT_END only for a print that is running (KAN-382,
# #93: a second press must not park an already parked head), so the cancel
# is sent from a print file. In batch mode virtual_sdcard only runs the file
# once this input is exhausted, so the SDCARD_PRINT_FILE must stay last; the
# file's one line cancels and then asserts (_CUT_TEST_CANCEL).
DICTIONARY atmega2560.dict
CONFIG cut_filament.cfg

G28
G90
G1 X100 Y100 Z5 F6000
G1 Z0.2 F600
CONTACT_GUARD_SIMULATE LOAD=0 DURATION=0.5
ASSERT_GUARD ENABLED=1 ACTIVE=1 CONTACT=0
_CUT_TEST

SDCARD_PRINT_FILE FILENAME=cancel_first_layer.gcode
